  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="467f4df7-d8b8-5cdf-8520-ab7434d0bd69" activityNameId="1b7dd117-0024-5372-a08f-1bd181cd8dc4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Funnel glass, CRT screen, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Funnel glass, CRT screen, at plant
A production site with a total life span of 50 a is assumed. Data are taken from a European IPCC BAT report about glass production. Data represent one example of a European production site.;
Synonyms: lead glass; 
UUID: 123bcdf7-254d-3211-ab73-72452d74d1a6
This module includes the material and energy efforts for: preparation and sorting of cullet, melting, forming of CRT funnel glass parts, cooling down, packaging and palletising until glass parts are ready for the next process step. Included are as well direct emissions to air, waste water and waste. Infrastructure and transport efforts of the input materials are estimated, based on packaging glass production.
Location: Date from one European production site used as global average data
Technology: current European production technology of CRT glass
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 525'000 t (CRT total, 1997)
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_123bcdf7-254d-3211-ab73-72452d74d1a6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
